# Build context for agent/Dockerfile.
#
# The image runs `COPY . .`, so anything left here is baked into it. `.env` is
# the one that matters: a developer's local file would be copied in and then read
# by `load_dotenv()` at import time, silently overriding the environment
# variables docker-compose passes to the container — including LIVEKIT_URL,
# which has to be the service name inside the network and 127.0.0.1 outside it.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

__pycache__/
*.pyc

.venv/
venv/

# Editor / vcs noise
.git
.gitignore
.DS_Store
.idea
.vscode
